of the schema","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"iglu:com.snowplowanalytics.snowplow\/payload_data\/jsonschema\/1-0-4"},{"text":", whose ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"data"},{"text":" is an array of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"events, one per record, oldest first. Every member of an event is a string, as the tracker","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"protocol has them:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Member","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Holds","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"aid","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The app ID the encoder is made with"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"co"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The standard context’s entities (below), as the text of a self-describing JSON array of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"contexts"},{"type":"text","text":"; left out when there are none"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"dtm","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"ttm","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"When the event was tracked, in epoch milliseconds","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"e","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"ue","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", a self-describing event","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"eid"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The record’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EventRecord\/id"},{"type":"text","text":", as a lowercase UUID; a redelivered record keeps it"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ip"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0.0.0.0"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"p"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The platform: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"mob"},{"type":"text","text":" for a phone, pad, watch or Vision Pro, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tv"},{"type":"text","text":" for an Apple TV, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"pc"},{"type":"text","text":" for a Mac, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"app"},{"type":"text","text":" when the record has no device in its context"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"sid","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The record’s session, its ","type":"text"},{"code":"SessionKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", as a lowercase UUID; left out when its context has no session","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tv"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"traffluent"},{"type":"text","text":", the tracker"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"ue_pr","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The event, as the text of a self-describing JSON ","type":"text"},{"code":"unstruct_event","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" holding the event’s own self-describing JSON: its schema, ","type":"text"},{"code":"iglu:<vendor>\/<name>\/jsonschema\/<version>-0-0","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and its data, its stored properties by name","type":"text"}]}]]],"type":"table","header":"row"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The session is the only identifier sent: there is no ","type":"text"},{"code":"duid","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"uid","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"nuid","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"tnuid","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"client_session","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" entity, whose ","type":"text"},{"code":"userId","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" lasts across sessions, and no ","type":"text"},{"code":"appleIdfv","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"appleIdfa","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"or other device identifier. Snowplow’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"domain_sessionid","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the session; a record with no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"session (one tracked by a tracker without ","type":"text"},{"code":"Enricher.sessions()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", or one a store recovered after","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a relaunch, which keeps no context) is sent without one, linked to nothing. The record’s vendor","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"identifier and trace context, and any other context value, aren’t sent.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Each event’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"ttm","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", its true timestamp, is the record’s timestamp, as is ","type":"text"},{"code":"dtm","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so Snowplow’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"derived_tstamp","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is when the event was tracked, uncorrected for the device’s clock. No ","type":"text"},{"code":"stm","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is sent: a retried request sends the same body again, so a sent time would be the first","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"attempt’s, and Snowplow would move the event later by however long the retries took.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The event’s schema is named after its "},{"code":"Event\/name","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"Event\/schemaVersion","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":": version N is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"SchemaVer "},{"code":"N-0-0","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Each version of an event is a breaking change, a SchemaVer MODEL. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"compatible change at the same version is an ADDITION, which the tracking plan’s Iglu export"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"code":"TrackingPlan\/writeIgluRegistry(to:vendor:registry:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":") writes for Iglu Server as "},{"code":"N-0-1","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"on, each superseding the ones before, so an event naming "},{"code":"N-0-0","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is validated against the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"newest of them. A static repository doesn’t supersede: there an event naming "},{"code":"N-0-0","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"validated against "},{"code":"N-0-0","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" alone, so the export refuses an addition for one, and a change to an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"event needs a new version."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Properties are read through the event’s schema in ","type":"text"},{"code":"plan","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", as ","type":"text"},{"code":"PropertyReader","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" reads them. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Sensitive"},{"text":" value is never sent, whatever the record reveals: the property is left","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"out, an element of an array is ","type":"text"},{"code":"null","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and one inside a type the plan can’t map is ","type":"text"},{"code":"null","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"data then validates against the event’s exported schema, which never requires a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Sensitive","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"property.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"co","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" holds these entities, for the keys the record’s context has values for:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Entity"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Keys","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Holds"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"iglu:com.snowplowanalytics.snowplow\/mobile_context\/jsonschema\/1-0-3","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DeviceKey"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OperatingSystemKey"},{"type":"text","text":", both; "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NetworkKey"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LocaleKey"},{"type":"text","text":" if present"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"osType"},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ios"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tvos"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"watchos"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"visionos"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"osx"},{"type":"text","text":"), "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"osVersion"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"deviceManufacturer"},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Apple Inc."},{"type":"text","text":"), "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"deviceModel"},{"type":"text","text":"; "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"networkType"},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"wifi"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"mobile"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"offline"},{"type":"text","text":"; left out for a wired or other connection); "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"language"},{"type":"text","text":", the locale’s language code"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"iglu:com.snowplowanalytics.mobile\/application\/jsonschema\/1-0-0","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"ApplicationKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", with both a version and a build","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"version"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"build"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]],"type":"table","header":"row"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A record the encoder can’t write is left out of the request, and the batch’s other records are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sent: one whose event and version "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"plan"},{"type":"text","text":" doesn’t describe, one whose event name Iglu doesn’t"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"take, one whose event isn’t "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Encodable"},{"type":"text","text":", one that holds a value JSON can’t, one whose timestamp"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is outside the years 0 to 9999, and one whose JSON is over 150,000 bytes"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowEncodingError","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":")."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" returns them as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SkippedRecord"},{"type":"text","text":"s, which "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" logs and reports"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"on its "},{"type":"codeVoi